    dmo:name "Gestational Diabetes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "gestational-diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "However, having gestational diabetes increases your risk of getting type 2 diabetes later in life." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you have gestational diabetes, you are more likely to develop type 2 diabetes later in life." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/high-blood-glucose-levels> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "High Blood Glucose Levels" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "高血糖水平在怀孕早期会损害胎儿，增加出生缺陷的风险。" ;
    dmo:name "High Blood Glucose Levels" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "high-blood-glucose-levels" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "High blood glucose levels can harm the baby during this early stage and increase the chance that your baby will have birth defects of any of these organs." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Pregnancy can make certain diabetes health problems worse, such as eye, heart, and kidney disease, especially if your blood glucose levels are too high." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/large-for-gestational-age-baby> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Large for Gestational Age Baby" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The document states that people with diabetes may have babies who are above average in size, which may lead to cesarean delivery." ;
    dmo:name "Large for Gestational Age Baby" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "large-for-gestational-age-baby" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People with diabetes may have babies who are above average in size. If your baby is above average in size, your health care team may recommend cesarean delivery NIH external link." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/physical-inactivity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Physical Inactivity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档建议每周至少150分钟中等强度身体活动，说明久坐是可干预的风险因素。" ;
    dmo:name "Physical Inactivity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "physical-inactivity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Try for at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity physical activity, such as brisk walking, each week." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/preeclampsia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Preeclampsia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The document states that people with diabetes have a greater chance of developing preeclampsia during pregnancy." ;
    dmo:name "Preeclampsia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "preeclampsia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "You also have a greater chance of developing preeclampsia NIH external link. In preeclampsia, your blood pressure goes up and you may have too much protein in your urine during the second half of pregnancy." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/smoking> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Smoking" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The document states that smoking increases the chance of stillbirth or preterm birth and recommends stopping as soon as possible." ;
    dmo:name "Smoking" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "smoking" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Smoking External link can increase your chance of having a stillborn baby or a baby born too early. Both smoking and diabetes can make your blood vessels narrow." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/type-2-diabetes> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Type 2 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Individuals with a history of gestational diabetes are at increased risk of developing type 2 diabetes later in life." ;
    dmo:name "Type 2 Diabetes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "type-2-diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you have gestational diabetes, you are more likely to develop type 2 diabetes later in life." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/high-blood-pressure> a dmo:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "High Blood Pressure" ;
    dmo:name "High Blood Pressure" ;
    dmo:symptomCode "high-blood-pressure" ;
    dmo:urgency "Urgent" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "You should also check your blood pressure or have it checked by a health care professional during the first 3 to 12 weeks after having your baby." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/low-blood-glucose-levels> a dmo:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "Low Blood Glucose Levels" ;
    dmo:name "Low Blood Glucose Levels" ;
    dmo:symptomCode "low-blood-glucose-levels" ;
    dmo:urgency "Urgent" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "You should also check your blood glucose levels often to watch for low blood glucose levels in the first few days." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-pregnancy-preexisting-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/worsening-of-diabetic-eye-disease> a dmo:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "Worsening of Diabetic Eye Disease" ;
    dmo:name "Worsening of Diabetic Eye Disease" ;
    dmo:symptomCode "worsening-of-diabetic-eye-disease" ;
    dmo:urgency "Urgent" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Diabetic eye disease may get worse after you have a baby." ;
